1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,789
Money in GTA 6 matters more than in

2
00:00:02,789 --> 00:00:05,579
any GTA before it. Guns, cars, clothes, all

3
00:00:05,579 --> 00:00:08,368
of it costs cash, and some story missions

4
00:00:08,368 --> 00:00:11,157
won't even start until you have enough of

5
00:00:11,157 --> 00:00:12,552
it in your pocket.

6
00:00:12,802 --> 00:00:14,980
So in this video I'll give you the

7
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:17,157
full money route from the early game to

8
00:00:17,157 --> 00:00:19,335
the mid game. What to do first, what

9
00:00:19,335 --> 00:00:21,512
to skip, and the one mistake that can

10
00:00:21,512 --> 00:00:23,690
wipe out everything you've earned in a single

11
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:23,962
second.

12
00:00:24,212 --> 00:00:27,188
Here's the plan. We'll cover how to protect

13
00:00:27,188 --> 00:00:30,164
your cash, the starter methods, Kenton's treasure diving,

14
00:00:30,164 --> 00:00:33,140
Moses and stolen cars, gang hideouts, high-end stores,

15
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:36,116
and finally the banks. Stick around for the

16
00:00:36,116 --> 00:00:39,092
money cheat at the end, because it's not

17
00:00:39,092 --> 00:00:40,580
what most people think.

18
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:43,332
Let's start with that mistake. At the beginning

19
00:00:43,332 --> 00:00:45,834
you don't have a bank account. Every dollar

20
00:00:45,834 --> 00:00:48,337
sits in your pocket, and if you die

21
00:00:48,337 --> 00:00:50,526
or get busted, that cash is gone.

22
00:00:50,776 --> 00:00:53,210
You unlock a bank account in the mission

23
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:55,644
Buck Me, roughly one to two hours into

24
00:00:55,644 --> 00:00:58,078
the game. Until then, here's a trick: you

25
00:00:58,078 --> 00:01:00,512
can hide cash under the loose floorboards in

26
00:01:00,512 --> 00:01:01,120
Jason's bedroom.

27
00:01:01,370 --> 00:01:04,116
And even after you have a bank, there's

28
00:01:04,116 --> 00:01:06,861
a rule. You can carry a maximum of

29
00:01:06,861 --> 00:01:09,607
twenty thousand dollars in cash. Anything above that

30
00:01:09,607 --> 00:01:12,352
goes straight into your BuckMe account. So after

31
00:01:12,352 --> 00:01:15,098
every big job, find an ATM and deposit.

32
00:01:15,348 --> 00:01:18,348
Now, earning. The first method is available right

33
00:01:18,348 --> 00:01:21,348
from the start: store stick-ups. Walk into any

34
00:01:21,348 --> 00:01:24,348
grocery store, point your gun at the cashier,

35
00:01:24,348 --> 00:01:27,348
and make them open the register. The police

36
00:01:27,348 --> 00:01:30,348
response is light, but so is the payout.

37
00:01:30,598 --> 00:01:32,792
The real money isn't in the register. It's

38
00:01:32,792 --> 00:01:34,987
in the safe in the back room. The

39
00:01:34,987 --> 00:01:37,181
code is often written on a Post-it note

40
00:01:37,181 --> 00:01:39,375
somewhere nearby, or you can scare it out

41
00:01:39,375 --> 00:01:40,198
of the clerk.

42
00:01:40,448 --> 00:01:43,310
This is where Focus Mode changes everything. Click

43
00:01:43,310 --> 00:01:46,172
both sticks at the same time. Cash glows

44
00:01:46,172 --> 00:01:49,034
green, useful items glow yellow, and notes with

45
00:01:49,034 --> 00:01:51,897
safe codes get highlighted. Doors tell you something

46
00:01:51,897 --> 00:01:54,759
too: white means you can go in, red

47
00:01:54,759 --> 00:01:55,832
means it's alarmed.

48
00:01:56,082 --> 00:01:58,782
Mugging is also open from the start, but

49
00:01:58,782 --> 00:02:01,481
honestly, it only gets you pocket change. I'd

50
00:02:01,481 --> 00:02:04,181
use stick-ups and muggings only when you need

51
00:02:04,181 --> 00:02:06,881
a little quick cash. Don't grind them for

52
00:02:06,881 --> 00:02:07,218
hours.

53
00:02:07,468 --> 00:02:10,337
One small purchase pays off on every robbery:

54
00:02:10,337 --> 00:02:13,207
a suppressor. Grab one from the Ammu-Nation in

55
00:02:13,207 --> 00:02:16,076
Key Lento right after the tutorial. Police respond

56
00:02:16,076 --> 00:02:18,945
to gunshot reports, so a suppressor buys you

57
00:02:18,945 --> 00:02:20,380
more time to loot.

58
00:02:20,630 --> 00:02:23,412
And the police in GTA 6 don't automatically

59
00:02:23,412 --> 00:02:26,194
know everything anymore. They track what you look

60
00:02:26,194 --> 00:02:28,976
like. Wear a hat and bandana during the

61
00:02:28,976 --> 00:02:31,758
crime, take them off after, keep a spare

62
00:02:31,758 --> 00:02:34,540
outfit in your trunk, switch cars, and destroy

63
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:36,974
the CCTV footage in the back room.

64
00:02:37,224 --> 00:02:40,003
Now the best early-game money. Kenton runs a

65
00:02:40,003 --> 00:02:42,782
scuba boat shop in Key Lento, with an

66
00:02:42,782 --> 00:02:45,561
illegal side business: underwater treasure diving. Jason does

67
00:02:45,561 --> 00:02:48,340
the diving, and in total it can earn

68
00:02:48,340 --> 00:02:50,424
you tens of thousands of dollars.

69
00:02:50,674 --> 00:02:53,300
It's not instant money, it takes time. But

70
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:55,926
whenever you're in Key Lento, squeeze in a

71
00:02:55,926 --> 00:02:58,552
dive. It runs alongside the story, and before

72
00:02:58,552 --> 00:03:00,850
you know it your account is full.

73
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:03,596
A simple habit that pays off: every time

74
00:03:03,596 --> 00:03:06,092
the story sends you down to Key Lento,

75
00:03:06,092 --> 00:03:08,588
plan a dive before you head back. You're

76
00:03:08,588 --> 00:03:11,084
already there, so it's free money for a

77
00:03:11,084 --> 00:03:12,644
few extra minutes of play.

78
00:03:12,894 --> 00:03:15,774
Your second big source is cars. In Chapter

79
00:03:15,774 --> 00:03:18,654
2 you meet Moses in Port Gellhorn. He

80
00:03:18,654 --> 00:03:21,534
buys stolen cars, but only ones without a

81
00:03:21,534 --> 00:03:21,894
tracker.

82
00:03:22,144 --> 00:03:24,785
How much does he pay? The guides disagree

83
00:03:24,785 --> 00:03:27,427
here. One says one to five thousand dollars

84
00:03:27,427 --> 00:03:30,068
per car, another says over ten thousand for

85
00:03:30,068 --> 00:03:32,709
a good one. Either way, the better the

86
00:03:32,709 --> 00:03:34,360
car, the bigger the payout.

87
00:03:34,610 --> 00:03:37,485
After a sale, Moses goes on cooldown. The

88
00:03:37,485 --> 00:03:40,360
fix is simple: sleep at a safehouse and

89
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:43,235
the cooldown resets. Pay N Spray also buys

90
00:03:43,235 --> 00:03:46,110
cars, but it has a daily limit and

91
00:03:46,110 --> 00:03:48,266
won't take high-end cars with trackers.

92
00:03:48,516 --> 00:03:51,007
Before you take a car, open the Waink

93
00:03:51,007 --> 00:03:53,498
app on your phone. It shows what security

94
00:03:53,498 --> 00:03:55,988
the car has, what it'll sell for, and

95
00:03:55,988 --> 00:03:58,479
what it costs to register. Steal blind and

96
00:03:58,479 --> 00:04:00,036
you might waste your time.

97
00:04:00,286 --> 00:04:03,025
Later on, in western Vice City, you meet

98
00:04:03,025 --> 00:04:05,764
Randy. He hands out contracts for high-end cars,

99
00:04:05,764 --> 00:04:08,502
which pay more, and he gives you a

100
00:04:08,502 --> 00:04:11,241
key cloner so you can steal keyless electronic

101
00:04:11,241 --> 00:04:11,926
cars too.

102
00:04:12,176 --> 00:04:14,980
Source number three is riskier, but it pays

103
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:17,785
well: rival gang hideouts. When you pass near

104
00:04:17,785 --> 00:04:20,589
one, a yellow icon appears on the map,

105
00:04:20,589 --> 00:04:23,393
and the map even tells you what's stashed

106
00:04:23,393 --> 00:04:23,744
inside.

107
00:04:23,994 --> 00:04:26,480
The drugs you find there vary a lot

108
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:28,965
in value. Weed is cheap, crystal and cocaine

109
00:04:28,965 --> 00:04:31,451
are worth far more. You have to carry

110
00:04:31,451 --> 00:04:33,936
them to a dealer yourself, someone like Tyrone,

111
00:04:33,936 --> 00:04:36,422
who pays you on the spot. You can

112
00:04:36,422 --> 00:04:38,907
drop them at a garage later instead, but

113
00:04:38,907 --> 00:04:41,082
then the dealer takes a bigger cut.

114
00:04:41,332 --> 00:04:44,077
Now the big scores. Before banks come high-end

115
00:04:44,077 --> 00:04:46,821
stores: the jewelry and clothing shops in Capri,

116
00:04:46,821 --> 00:04:49,566
Ocean Beach and Downtown Vice City. Security is

117
00:04:49,566 --> 00:04:52,311
tighter, so scout them on the map first

118
00:04:52,311 --> 00:04:55,056
to see how much loot there is and

119
00:04:55,056 --> 00:04:56,428
how heavily they're guarded.

120
00:04:56,678 --> 00:04:59,311
Medium and high security jobs are much easier

121
00:04:59,311 --> 00:05:01,943
as a duo. Invite your partner from the

122
00:05:01,943 --> 00:05:04,576
map icon. Go in through the back door

123
00:05:04,576 --> 00:05:07,208
with a snap gun and the alarm stays

124
00:05:07,208 --> 00:05:09,841
quiet. Each character carries two stash bags, a

125
00:05:09,841 --> 00:05:12,474
van or truck holds up to eight, and

126
00:05:12,474 --> 00:05:13,790
a motorbike holds none.

127
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:16,742
To sell the jewelry, head to Yasmani in

128
00:05:16,742 --> 00:05:19,444
Little Cuba. He pays well for jewelry and

129
00:05:19,444 --> 00:05:22,147
marked bills. And remember, loot isn't money until

130
00:05:22,147 --> 00:05:23,160
you've sold it.

131
00:05:23,410 --> 00:05:26,020
Then come the banks. They open up roughly

132
00:05:26,020 --> 00:05:28,630
halfway through the story. Banks use dye packs

133
00:05:28,630 --> 00:05:31,240
that explode, so you'll need a dye pack

134
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:33,850
jammer first, which you get in Chapter 3.

135
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:36,724
A bank has three targets: the tellers' cash

136
00:05:36,724 --> 00:05:39,348
drawers, safes full of marked bills, and the

137
00:05:39,348 --> 00:05:41,972
vault, where the biggest money is. But the

138
00:05:41,972 --> 00:05:44,596
moment you walk out, your wanted level goes

139
00:05:44,596 --> 00:05:47,220
straight up. It's the biggest payday in the

140
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:48,860
game, and the biggest risk.

141
00:05:49,110 --> 00:05:51,530
So before any bank job, plan the exit,

142
00:05:51,530 --> 00:05:53,950
not just the entry. Park a fast car

143
00:05:53,950 --> 00:05:56,370
you haven't been seen in nearby, know where

144
00:05:56,370 --> 00:05:58,790
you'll change your outfit, and deposit the cash

145
00:05:58,790 --> 00:06:01,210
the moment you're clear. The vault means nothing

146
00:06:01,210 --> 00:06:03,630
if you lose it all in the chase.

147
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:07,144
So where should the money go? My order

148
00:06:07,144 --> 00:06:10,408
is simple. First, savings for story missions, because

149
00:06:10,408 --> 00:06:13,672
some won't unlock without the cash. Then weapons.

150
00:06:13,672 --> 00:06:16,528
Then cars and upgrades. Clothes come last.

151
00:06:16,778 --> 00:06:19,509
And here's something a lot of players don't

152
00:06:19,509 --> 00:06:22,241
know: you can't buy houses or safehouses in

153
00:06:22,241 --> 00:06:24,972
GTA 6. The story gives you places to

154
00:06:24,972 --> 00:06:27,362
live. So don't save up for property.

155
00:06:27,612 --> 00:06:30,211
And yes, there is a money cheat. It

156
00:06:30,211 --> 00:06:32,810
gives you two hundred and fifty thousand dollars

157
00:06:32,810 --> 00:06:35,409
every time, but it only unlocks after you

158
00:06:35,409 --> 00:06:36,708
finish the main story.

159
00:06:36,958 --> 00:06:39,832
The catch: with cheats on, you can't save,

160
00:06:39,832 --> 00:06:42,706
trophies and achievements are disabled, and the money

161
00:06:42,706 --> 00:06:45,579
vanishes when you quit. So there's no shortcut

162
00:06:45,579 --> 00:06:48,094
early on. You have to earn it.

163
00:06:48,344 --> 00:06:51,281
Before the recap, three mistakes I see new

164
00:06:51,281 --> 00:06:54,218
players make. Mistake one: carrying a big pile

165
00:06:54,218 --> 00:06:57,155
of cash into a fight. If the job

166
00:06:57,155 --> 00:07:00,092
goes wrong, that money is gone. Deposit first,

167
00:07:00,092 --> 00:07:01,928
then go looking for trouble.

168
00:07:02,178 --> 00:07:04,775
Mistake two: robbing a store with your face

169
00:07:04,775 --> 00:07:07,372
showing and then driving off in the same

170
00:07:07,372 --> 00:07:09,969
car. The police remember your look and your

171
00:07:09,969 --> 00:07:12,566
vehicle. A hat, a bandana and a quick

172
00:07:12,566 --> 00:07:14,514
car swap make a huge difference.

173
00:07:14,764 --> 00:07:17,711
Mistake three: grinding small jobs for hours. Muggings

174
00:07:17,711 --> 00:07:20,658
and stick-ups are fine for a little quick

175
00:07:20,658 --> 00:07:23,606
cash, but the real money is in Kenton's

176
00:07:23,606 --> 00:07:26,553
dives, Moses's cars, and later the big stores

177
00:07:26,553 --> 00:07:29,500
and banks. Play the story to unlock them.

178
00:07:29,750 --> 00:07:32,890
Quick recap. Early on, a few stick-ups and

179
00:07:32,890 --> 00:07:36,030
Moses's car contracts. Start treasure diving as soon

180
00:07:36,030 --> 00:07:39,170
as you meet Kenton. Hit gang hideouts when

181
00:07:39,170 --> 00:07:42,310
you see the yellow icon. Before banks, the

182
00:07:42,310 --> 00:07:45,450
high-end stores in Capri and Ocean Beach. And

183
00:07:45,450 --> 00:07:48,590
in the mid game, banks and Randy's contracts.

184
00:07:48,840 --> 00:07:51,490
And the most important rule of all: after

185
00:07:51,490 --> 00:07:54,139
every big job, put your money in an

186
00:07:54,139 --> 00:07:56,789
ATM. One bad chase and your pocket is

187
00:07:56,789 --> 00:07:57,120
empty.

188
00:07:57,370 --> 00:07:59,887
If you only remember one thing from this

189
00:07:59,887 --> 00:08:02,403
video, make it this: the safest money in

190
00:08:02,403 --> 00:08:04,920
GTA 6 is the money in your bank,

191
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:06,178
not in your pocket.

192
00:08:06,428 --> 00:08:08,993
Now tell me, what's the best money method

193
00:08:08,993 --> 00:08:11,559
you've found in GTA 6 so far? Drop

194
00:08:11,559 --> 00:08:14,124
it in the comments, and if this guide

195
00:08:14,124 --> 00:08:16,689
helped, subscribe. Next video, we're ranking the best

196
00:08:16,689 --> 00:08:17,972
cars in the game.
